==Restrictions==
Deploy from Row 1 only

==Battleground==
*2 [[Professor A.|Professor As]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 143.33~146.67 seconds<sup>4,300f~4,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 14.67~21.33 seconds<sup>440f~640f</sup>.
*1 [[Queen Mother V]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*3 [[One Horn]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 56~58.67 seconds<sup>1,680f~1,760f</sup>.
*1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 12~16 seconds<sup>360f~480f</sup>.

==Strategy==
I'll Big Bug is just a copy of [[I'll Be Bug (Merciless)|I'll Be Bug]], though a 5-slot restriction cuts down on the amount of options you can use. In practice, however, [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] already do most of the heavy lifting in the original stage, so the stage plays very similarly to the original. In fact, you can even use the remaining two slots for a Cat Combo despite the restriction, simply because the aforementioned three cats are already so good for the stage. The addition of [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] to your arsenal provides another strong option for the stage. Overall,  the restriction shouldn't change things much.

==='''Key Units'''===
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: As with the previous stage, Roe Cat has the health to act as a tank against Professor A. with its Resistance and has a 20% Weaken chance against Red enemies for support, making it crucial for the stage. As always, time it properly to avoid Queen Mother V's attacks. Recommended Lv.40 or above.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Having LD attacks, high speed and Massive Damage against Reds, Courier can be used to quickly whittle down One Horns and Ginger Snaches (if they don't get into its blindspot) for other units to focus on taking out Professor A. While Roe's weaken is not always reliable, when it does trigger a level 40+ Courier can actually hit Professor A for huge damage.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Awakened Bahamut Cat's high burst damage is very useful here. He would be a big source of damage to Professor A. with proper timing, especially if aided by Roe's anti-Red weaken/Thunderbolt. His speed helps him to evade Queen Mother V's attacks. Bahamut's most useful role here is actually wiping out the Relic Doges, relieving the pressure exerted on Roe Cat and retaining your momentum. Be wary of his low range and health.

==='''Useful Units'''===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can's very high damage, low cost and Extra Money talent all help in picking off the annoying peons, but should not be relied upon when fighting Professor A.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Thanks to its incredibly high speed, Bullet Train continues to be a useful chipper that can guarantee at least one hit on Professor A. if the path is clear. It also comes into use at sniping other peons should the need arises.
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]]: Manic Island continues to serve as a cost-effective anti-Red specialist that is strong against them, although the lack of combos if opting for it can reduce its effectiveness.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Unlocked from the previous stage, Slime Cat possesses a devastating Wave Attack that can provide a lot of value. But make sure to time them well. Thunderbolt Cannon is useful to force a hit in.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]]: Neo Cutter Cat can burst out a ton of damage onto the Red enemies in this stage. You can even consider his [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Attack Combo]].
*Defense Up Cat Combos: Despite this stage's restriction, your Key Units put in so much work that you could consider using a 2-slot Defense Up combo such as [[Étoile minimum (Combo)|Étoile minimum]] or [[Little Warriors (Combo)|Little Warriors]] to ensure Courier Cat can get more attacks in.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
''Generally, any Uber that works well in I'll Be Bug should work well here''
*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai DX]]: Bane of red enemies, being able to quickly squash the One Horns and Professor As. Just make sure to protect her from the Relic Doges and get her inside the boss' blindspot. You must time her very well and guard her from the Ginger Snaches&mdash;a knockback could mean instant loss.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Single-target DPS unit that basically acts as a better Can Can and is insidiously effective. He works very well with his Strengthen/Cost Down Talents to wipe out the One Horns as well as the Relic Doges, while being replaceable easily if lost. His weakness to Professor A. is at worst trivial given his low range and how most strategies account for them already, making him an excellent choice.
*[[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kuu γ]]: Pai-Pai lite. Tanks red units and dishes out considerable damage back to them as [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x9E3XxqsF90 demonstrated by Lucas IV]. She can even have Curse Immunity with Talents, although the effects of doing so is negligible.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Though vulnerable to Curse, Phonoa's very high speed (30), far-reaching LD multi-hits and huge standing range (600 vs 501) means it can utterly reduce every enemy in the stage to rubble. It still requires a fair bit of support to hold its own within the blindspot, but it usually isn't much of an issue.
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]]: As long as Cat Machine is not cursed, Cat Machine will whittle down Queen Mother V's and Professor A's health. A level 40 Cat Machine can survive long enough for another Cat Machine, allowing for stacking. Speed up talents and combos are recommended.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Hyper Battalion Convoys]]: Essentially a much stronger Roe, Convoys can easily infiltrate Queen Mother V's blind spot and prevent Professor A. from attacking your other units by constantly knocking him back, allowing your other units free rein to attack the vulnerable Mother V with barely any resistance. Make sure it doesn't get cursed, though.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)| Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Curse immune, decent speed (16), and freeze & strong against relic and red enemies make her absolutely busted in this stage. Her strong against ability especially means she has incredible bulk and exceeds Dasli levels of DPS at the same level.
*Talented [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]]: With target relic and curse immune talents unlocked, Ruri completely breaks this stage by solo tanking all enemies in the stage (red and relic), while also applying weaken. With high enough levels, Ruri can solo the level with no help.
*[[Ken (Uber Rare Cat)|Crimson King of Battle Ken]]: If you happen to own this unit, it will be a massive help for this stage, as it is fast enough to easily infiltrate Queen Mother V's blindspot, and is also immune to Professor A.'s slow and can weaken and is strong against almost every threat in this stage.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: Fast enough to infiltrate Queen Mother V's blind spot and deal insane damage to everything in the stage. Additionally, immune to curse. Just watch out for his health, as Prof. A outranges unless he has a stepping stone.
*[[Victorious Skanda (Uber Rare Cat)|Victorious Skanda]]: This unit acts like a second Thunderbolt cannon that can be easily used alongside [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], plus Skanda can weaken red enemies and has a level 2 wave attack as a bonus.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]]: While still vulnerable to the Red peons in this stage, his Conjure can help relief the pressure of this stage and push the enemies back to the base. Both his forms work, however, his Evolved Form is preferred for extra bulk to make it to the frontlines.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]]: Like is counterpart, his Conjure is very valuable in this stage, sacrificing cost and Knockback for quick, high damage burst with his conjurer. His Extra Money ability also helps when sniping peons with his Wave Attack, letting you burst professor A. down. While he can only usually get one or two hits in himself, his damage is not bad when Strengthened at 50% on his second repositon.
*[[King of Extinction Phono]]: Just like in the original stage, he destroys everything if he will slide into Queen Mother V’s blindspot.

